.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt MESG 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mesg
.Nd control terminal write permission
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl t Ar path
.Op y | n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reports whether other users may write to the current terminal.
With
.Ql y
it allows writes and with
.Ql n
it refuses them by changing the terminal's group-write bit through the
.Pa tty:
control protocol.
The setting is persistent for the console/session and only root may change it.
.Pp
The
.Fl t
option selects another terminal path; it is a RavenBSD extension for testing.
A path that is not a character device reports
.Dq not a tty
and exits 1.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t Ar path
Use
.Ar path
instead of
.Pa tty:console .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
The query exits 0 when writes are allowed and 1 when they are refused.
A failed set or usage error exits non-zero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr stty 1 ,
.Xr tty 1
.Sh STANDARDS
IEEE Std 1003.1-2024
.Pq POSIX.1-2024 .
